<description>&lt;p&gt;Mexican special forces, aided by U.S. surveillance drones, raided a home in northern Sinaloa and captured cartel leader El Chapo Isidro, while no U.S. agents were on site. During the raid Mexican soldiers were attacked, resulting in eleven deaths and vehicles set ablaze on a highway, and the operation disrupted a local baseball match. The United States has requested extradition of El Chapo Isidro, and the capture has sparked a risk of a violent succession battle within the cartel. 37 battle-related deaths were recorded in 1996, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxOUm9KTnF2aG4xTXRUYWZGeDgycjZwSElpWXYxQ09uX1FuQVMxMUcyUXdEdWxKbVR5M09Ja2pSa3A0dzM4VkFOVFdlQWJXbVlTWk1oVFV2cmc5YWFzU3BxdUV5SE0xck4ydndUZ0lyVzhWNmJqaVN1RTc1Qk11X2hNVzgtNUZib0FtV3ktN2ZzdGc3blR1T1VZRlpUYVNSY1oyMXgzREtIQ0FfdGo2WDVNcGdrVEVleUltNG5sRWtWdi03dw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxQTHF2OGxlbDVVLWlUbV9rbFludTRBd3FZYmpvdGdrSU85WFNydlRlOFg5UFJuUDVDMDl0Vk14bGMtOUg0Y25ZMU5rVXlFc1lCaGs4WlJudWpMTWktYUc5dWxxeUFCMzVTMTNqc3JscGxvVldLQXJFdUxmbTd6SGlfMUJrNDVqTW5UWFhGc0J0UldDdUx2Nmd1Qkx5NWRBaVU2TENFNjJLSWlFNmJTQnpyQzVqM3hVRnp2a05nQnFMQ19KZHBwcU9hWA?oc=5&quot;&gt;AP News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxPa3pZM1VTZlNaNW8wZDQ4SmdIcjItTG9NTXNBQ0RWQ0V3NjJlY0xrdF8zaWx1ZS12eGV6dkFHbC1FN3NaczN4eC1aY2J5dHMzWmFmWVhOZDE5dG5jZEJaY3Q1bjc1NzlwTkg4a092U3JiRU85c0x6U1B6LXdlYkthdThUN21aMk5yM1hhRFBCNXBJeHR3VEhfMjZCSHI?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxPdTJWOWx0TWc0em5CMlg1QlM3TXM4UndMM3JoekpiMnpBekw5eUNPRTB4a0sxd0ZmSmsyelh2NE5CdnpGaF9lSnlqX25TSl9LSWJQaWlrVVJYcGxIdHdPSFhtMlNpS